# VPSGUI Environment Variables
#
# Copy to .env.local for local overrides. Every VITE_* value is inlined into the client bundle at
# BUILD time and is publicly readable - never put secrets here. The agent token is entered by the
# operator at runtime under Settings -> Agent Token and lives only in browser localStorage.

# REST API base URL.
# Leave unset in production: the client then derives `${window.location.origin}/api/v1`, which the
# bundled nginx config proxies to the agent on 127.0.0.1:46509.
# For local development against an agent on this machine, point straight at it:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:46509/api/v1

# Telemetry WebSocket URL.
# Leave unset. The bundled vpsgui-agent is a plain HTTP daemon with no WebSocket endpoint, and the
# UI polls REST telemetry instead. Set this only if you run a custom backend that speaks the
# telemetry socket protocol.
# VITE_WS_URL=
